<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block line-height="1">Since damage to text witnesses frequently makes them harder to read, the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.damage" text-decoration="underline">&lt;damage&gt;</basic-link> element will often contain an <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> element. If the damaged area is not continuous (e.g. a stain affecting several strings of text), the <inline font-style="italic">group</inline> attribute may be used to group together several related <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.damage" text-decoration="underline">&lt;damage&gt;</basic-link> elements; alternatively the <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;join&gt;</inline> element may be used to indicate which <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.damage" text-decoration="underline">&lt;damage&gt;</basic-link> and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> elements are part of the same physical phenomenon.</block><block line-height="1" text-indent="1em" space-before.optimum="0pt" space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.damage" text-decoration="underline">&lt;damage&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.del" text-decoration="underline">&lt;del&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.supplied" text-decoration="underline">&lt;supplied&gt;</basic-link> elements may be closely allied in use. See section <basic-link external-destination="url(https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html#PHCOMB)">12.3.3.2. Use of the gap, del, damage, unclear, and supplied Elements in Combination</basic-link> for discussion of which element is appropriate for which circumstance.</block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Example</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt"><inline>&lt;l&gt;</inline>The Moving Finger wri<inline>&lt;damage agent="water" group="1"&gt;</inline>es; and<inline>&lt;/damage&gt;</inline> having writ,<inline>&lt;/l&gt;</inline>
<inline>&lt;l&gt;</inline>Moves <inline>&lt;damage agent="water" group="1"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;supplied&gt;</inline>on: nor all your<inline>&lt;/supplied&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/damage&gt;</inline> Piety nor Wit<inline>&lt;/l&gt;</inline></block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Content model</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt">
&lt;content&gt;
 &lt;macroRef key="macro.paraContent"/&gt;
&lt;/content&gt;
    </block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Schema Declaration</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt">
element damage
{
