<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">May contain</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Character data only</block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block line-height="1">The name <inline color="black" font-family="Helvetica">g</inline> is short for <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">gaiji</inline>, which is the Japanese term for a non-standardized character or glyph.</block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Example</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt"><inline>&lt;g ref="#ctlig"&gt;</inline>ct<inline>&lt;/g&gt;</inline></block>This example points to a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.glyph" text-decoration="underline">&lt;glyph&gt;</basic-link> element with the identifier <inline font-family="Courier">ctlig</inline> like the following: <block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt"><inline>&lt;glyph xml:id="ctlig"&gt;</inline>
<inline>&lt;!-- here we describe the particular ct-ligature intended --&gt;</inline>
<inline>&lt;/glyph&gt;</inline></block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Example</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt"><inline>&lt;g ref="#per-glyph"&gt;</inline>per<inline>&lt;/g&gt;</inline></block>The medieval brevigraph per could similarly be considered as an individual glyph, defined in a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.glyph" text-decoration="underline">&lt;glyph&gt;</basic-link> element with the identifier <inline font-family="Courier">per-glyph</inline> as follows: <block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt"><inline>&lt;glyph xml:id="per-glyph"&gt;</inline>
<inline>&lt;!-- ... --&gt;</inline>
<inline>&lt;/glyph&gt;</inline></block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Content model</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt">
&lt;content&gt;
 &lt;textNode/&gt;
&lt;/content&gt;
    </block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Schema Declaration</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt">
element g
{
   tei_att.global.attributes,
   tei_att.typed.attributes,
   attribute ref { text }?,
   text
}</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table>
<block keep-with-next.within-page="always" id="TEI.gap" text-align="left" font-family="Times" font-size="14pt" font-weight="bold" space-after="3pt" space-before.optimum="9pt" text-indent="0em">1.158. &lt;gap&gt;</block><table text-align="left" font-size="9pt" id="d27e128862"><table-column column-number="1" column-width="25%"/><table-column column-number="2" column-width="75%"/><table-body text-indent="0pt">
<table-row><table-cell number-columns-spanned="2" border-before-style="solid" border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">&lt;gap&gt; </inline>(gap) indicates a point where material has been omitted in a transcription, whether for editorial reasons described in the TEI header, as part of sampling practice, or because the material is illegible, invisible, or inaudible. [<basic-link external-destination="url(https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/CO.html#COEDADD)">3.5.3. Additions, Deletions, and Omissions</basic-link>]</block></table-cell></table-row>
