<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Example</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block font-family="Courier" background-color="lightgray" color="black" white-space-treatment="preserve" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" wrap-option="no-wrap" text-indent="0em" hyphenate="false" start-indent="12pt" text-align="start" font-size="6pt" space-before.optimum="4pt" space-after.optimum="4pt"><inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline> 
 The <inline>&lt;objectName ref="#MinsterLovellJewel"&gt;</inline>Minster Lovell Jewel<inline>&lt;/objectName&gt;</inline> is probably the most similar to the
<inline>&lt;objectName ref="#AlfredJewel"&gt;</inline>Alfred Jewel<inline>&lt;/objectName&gt;</inline> and was found in <inline>&lt;placeName ref="#MinsterLovell"&gt;</inline>Minster
   Lovell<inline>&lt;/placeName&gt;</inline> in <inline>&lt;placeName ref="#Oxfordshire"&gt;</inline>Oxfordshire<inline>&lt;/placeName&gt;</inline> and is kept at the <inline>&lt;orgName ref="#AshmoleanMuseum"&gt;</inline>Ashmolean Museum<inline>&lt;/orgName&gt;</inline>.
<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline></block></block></table-cell></table-row>
