<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>target</block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>supplies a pointer to the base being glossed by this ruby text.<table text-align="left" font-size="9pt" id="d27e301244"><table-column column-number="1" column-width="20%"/><table-column column-number="2" column-width="80%"/><table-body text-indent="0pt">
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Status</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Optional</block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Datatype</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teidata.pointer" text-decoration="underline">teidata.pointer</basic-link></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Schematron</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Enforce that <inline font-style="italic">either</inline> <inline font-style="italic">target</inline> or both <inline font-style="italic">from</inline> and <inline font-style="italic">to</inline> (or none) are used, but not <inline font-style="italic">target</inline> in combination with either <inline font-style="italic">from</inline> or <inline font-style="italic">to</inline>.<block>
&lt;sch:rule context="tei:rt/@target"&gt;
&lt;sch:report test="../@from | ../@to"&gt;When @target is present, neither @from nor @to should be.&lt;/sch:report&gt;
&lt;/sch:rule&gt;</block></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block line-height="1">Should point to a single <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.rb" text-decoration="underline">&lt;rb&gt;</basic-link> or an element that is inside an <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.rb" text-decoration="underline">&lt;rb&gt;</basic-link>. To refer to multiple elements or text nodes at once use <inline font-style="italic">from</inline> and <inline font-style="italic">to</inline>.</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>from</block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>points to the starting point of the span of text being glossed by this ruby text.<table text-align="left" font-size="9pt" id="d27e301318"><table-column column-number="1" column-width="20%"/><table-column column-number="2" column-width="80%"/><table-body text-indent="0pt">
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Status</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Optional</block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Datatype</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teidata.pointer" text-decoration="underline">teidata.pointer</basic-link></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Schematron</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Enforce the presence of <inline font-style="italic">to</inline> iff there is a <inline font-style="italic">from</inline>.<block>
&lt;sch:rule context="tei:rt/@from"&gt;
&lt;sch:assert test="../@to"&gt;When @from is present, the @to attribute of &lt;&lt;sch:name/&gt;&gt; is required.&lt;/sch:assert&gt;
&lt;/sch:rule&gt;</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>to</block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>points to the ending point of the span of text being glossed.<table text-align="left" font-size="9pt" id="d27e301356"><table-column column-number="1" column-width="20%"/><table-column column-number="2" column-width="80%"/><table-body text-indent="0pt">
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Status</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Optional</block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Datatype</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teidata.pointer" text-decoration="underline">teidata.pointer</basic-link></block></table-cell></table-row>
<table-row><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Schematron</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block>Enforce the presence of <inline font-style="italic">from</inline> iff there is a <inline font-style="italic">to</inline>.<block>
&lt;sch:rule context="tei:rt/@to"&gt;
&lt;sch:assert test="../@from"&gt;When @to is present, the @from attribute of &lt;&lt;sch:name/&gt;&gt; is required.&lt;/sch:assert&gt;
&lt;/sch:rule&gt;</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table></block></table-cell></table-row>
