<table-row><table-cell number-columns-spanned="2" border-before-style="solid" border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">&lt;vRange&gt; </inline>(value range) defines the range of allowed values for a feature, in the form of an <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.fs" text-decoration="underline">&lt;fs&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.vAlt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;vAlt&gt;</basic-link>, or primitive value; for the value of an <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.f" text-decoration="underline">&lt;f&gt;</basic-link> to be valid, it must be subsumed by the specified range; if the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.f" text-decoration="underline">&lt;f&gt;</basic-link> contains multiple values (as sanctioned by the <inline font-style="italic">org</inline> attribute), then each value must be subsumed by the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.vRange" text-decoration="underline">&lt;vRange&gt;</basic-link>. [<basic-link external-destination="url(https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/FS.html#FD)">19.11. Feature System Declaration</basic-link>]</block></table-cell></table-row>
