<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block line-height="1">If both <inline font-style="italic">when</inline> and <inline font-style="italic">dur</inline> or <inline font-style="italic">dur-iso</inline> are specified, the values should be interpreted as indicating a span of time by its starting time (or date) and duration. In order to represent a time range by a duration and its ending time the <inline font-style="italic">when-iso</inline> attribute must be used.</block><block line-height="1" text-indent="1em" space-before.optimum="0pt" space-before.maximum="12pt">In providing a ‘regularized’ form, no claim is made that the form in the source text is incorrect; the regularized form is simply that chosen as the main form for purposes of unifying variant forms under a single heading.</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table>
<block keep-with-next.within-page="always" id="TEI.att.duration.w3c" text-align="left" font-family="Times" font-size="14pt" font-weight="bold" space-after="3pt" space-before.optimum="9pt" text-indent="0em">3.25. att.duration.w3c</block><table text-align="left" font-size="9pt" id="d27e416648"><table-column column-number="1" column-width="25%"/><table-column column-number="2" column-width="75%"/><table-body text-indent="0pt">
