<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block line-height="1">A point is defined by two or three numeric values separated by commas. The numeric values should be expressed as decimal numbers which do not end in a decimal point. E.g., both <inline>0.0,84.2</inline> and <inline>0,84</inline> are allowed, but <inline>0.,84.</inline> is not.</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table>
