<table-row><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline></block></table-cell><table-cell border-after-style="solid" border-end-style="solid" border-start-style="solid" padding="2pt" text-align="left"><block><block line-height="1">This datatype is used to constrain a string of characters to one that can be used as a URI scheme name according to <basic-link external-destination="url(https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3986.txt)">RFC 3986</basic-link>, <basic-link external-destination="url(https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986#section-3.1)">section 3.1</basic-link>. Thus only the 26 lowercase letters a–z, the 10 digits 0–9, the plus sign, the period, and the hyphen are permitted, and the value must start with a letter.</block></block></table-cell></table-row></table-body></table>
